-- title:
--   Units on W ∩ Xₜ near a DVR point are units times powers of t
-- statement:
--   Let $X$ be a scheme, $t \in \Gamma(X, \mathcal{O}_X)$ a global section and $\xi \in X$ a point whose local ring $\mathcal{O}_{X,\xi}$ is a domain and a discrete valuation ring, and assume that the maximal ideal of $\mathcal{O}_{X,\xi}$ is the principal ideal generated by the germ of $t$ at $\xi$. Let $W \subseteq X$ be open with $\xi \in W$, and let $u \in \Gamma(W \cap X_t, \mathcal{O}_X)$ be a unit of that ring, where $X_t$ denotes the basic open subset of $X$ attached to $t$. The assertion is that there exist an open $W' \subseteq W$ with $\xi \in W'$, natural numbers $a, b$ and a unit $v \in \Gamma(W', \mathcal{O}_X)$ such that, after restricting everything to $W' \cap X_t$ (restricting $t$ from $X$ itself, $u$ along $W' \cap X_t \subseteq W \cap X_t$, and $v$ along $W' \cap X_t \subseteq W'$), one has $u \cdot t^{a} = v \cdot t^{b}$ in $\Gamma(W' \cap X_t, \mathcal{O}_X)$. Since $t$ is invertible on $X_t$, this says that $u = v\, t^{\,b-a}$ there; the statement is an equality of products of powers, so no sign of $b-a$ is asserted.
--
--   This is the local structure statement that a unit on the complement of the divisor of a local parameter $t$, near a point where the local ring is a discrete valuation ring with uniformiser the germ of $t$, becomes on a smaller neighbourhood a unit of the ambient ring times an integral power of $t$. It is used in the construction of local trivialisations of modules over such a scheme, being cited by [`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.exists_basicOpen_le_mem_nonempty_pullback_iso_of_nonempty_iso_unit_of_isDiscreteValuationRing_stalk`](thm.html#AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.exists_basicOpen_le_mem_nonempty_pullback_iso_of_nonempty_iso_unit_of_isDiscreteValuationRing_stalk).
